.SH NAME
ssoossh-service-retrieve - Retrieve a service certificate using a previously issued enrollment code.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh service retrieve [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Redeems an enrollment code from \fBservice enroll\fR, writing the certificate to -cert.pub and checking local disk to avoid unnecessary server calls.

.PP
The certificate is skipped (exit 0) if one at -cert.pub is valid beyond --grace (default 1 minute) unless --force is passed. If retrieval fails but a still-valid certificate exists, a warning is printed and exit 0 is returned (so \fBMatch exec\fR does not block SSH when the server is temporarily unreachable). Only when there is no readable, valid certificate does an error return a non-zero exit.

.PP
The key files follow OpenSSH naming: the private key is , the public key is \&.pub, and the certificate is -cert.pub.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--code\fP=""
	enrollment code (required)

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	retrieve a new certificate even if a valid one exists on disk

.PP
\fB--grace\fP="1m"
	duration of additional validity required before refreshing (default 1m); e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for retrieve

.PP
\fB--key\fP=""
	keypair path (relative or absolute; required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to the ssoossh config file

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address including scheme (e.g. "https://example.com") assumes https if omited.

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


